//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MTF Fractals + Stage · v6 · calibrated for XAUUSD and BTCUSD
//
// What it does
//   • Williams fractals (swing highs / swing lows) on the chart TF and on
//     5m / 15m / 1H / 4H / D / W. Right side strict, so a fractal can never be
//     broken on the bar that confirms it; equal extremes allowed on the left
//     (input) so double tops / bottoms at a tied price register.
//   • The most recent fractal of each side on each TF gets a stage:
//       Confirmed    – fractal confirmed on this TF's latest bar (higher TFs: on
//                      the previous closed bar of that TF; a higher-TF row shows
//                      Retest instead while the chart bar is back in the band)
//       Holding      – no close through the level yet; chart price is outside the
//                      retest band or has not left it since the fractal printed
//       Retest       – level intact, the chart bar's range reaches into the retest
//                      band after a bar has been entirely outside it at least once
//                      (also shown after a failed break)
//       Broken       – this TF's close went through the level by more than the
//                      break buffer; stays until the next fractal of that side
//       Flip retest  – level broken earlier, a chart bar has left the band and the
//                      current bar's range is back inside it (support ⇄ resistance)
//       Failed break – level was broken, then this TF's close went back through it
//                      by more than the break buffer; sticky until the next fractal
//                      (shows Retest whenever the chart bar is inside the band)
//   • Every higher-TF value (level, ATR, break state, age) comes from COMPLETED
//     bars of that TF ([1] offset + lookahead_on), so the table is identical on
//     history and in real time. Break / Failed break are judged on that TF's own
//     close; Retest / Flip retest use the live chart bar.
//   • The Chart row confirms fractals, updates its level and stage and fires its
//     fractal / break alerts only on the bar close (input), so they cannot appear
//     intrabar and vanish. Its Retest alert is a range event and fires at once.
//   • Bias (data window, table column, optional tint): +1 per enabled TF whose
//     last swing high is Broken / Flip retest, −1 per TF whose last swing low is
//     Broken / Flip retest; intact levels, Retest and Failed break count 0.
//     NOTE: opposite sign to the v5 script, which scored intact levels and so
//     read bearish on an upside breakout. Re-create anything built on the old
//     "MTF fractal bias" value.
//   • Rows whose TF is lower than the chart TF, equal to it, or not a whole
//     multiple of it are hidden (request.security cannot return them reliably);
//     the Σ row tooltip lists them. Tick charts hide all higher-TF rows and skip
//     the rollover filter.
//
// Calibration
//   Distances are measured in ATR(14) of the timeframe they belong to, so one
//   multiplier means the same thing on $4,000 gold and $80,000 bitcoin and on
//   5m as on D. The v5 fixed 0.15 % band equalled ~0.5 × ATR on 1H gold and was
//   far too tight on BTC and on D / W. Its fixed-percent width survives as
//   "Percent" mode; the stage logic above is the same in both modes.
//       retest band   ±0.50 × √(row ATR × chart ATR), never narrower than the
//                     break buffer   a pullback to the level, not every bar; on
//                     the Chart row this is 0.5 × ATR, and a D level seen from a
//                     5m chart gets a band a few 5m-ATRs wide instead of half a
//                     daily range
//       break buffer   0.15 × row ATR, floored at 0.012 % of the level (≈ $0.50
//                     on gold, one quiet-hours spread) so a close inside the
//                     spread never counts as Broken in thin sessions
//       fractal        2 / 2   classic Williams
//   After ATR normalisation XAUUSD and BTCUSD need the same multipliers, so the
//   inputs apply to every symbol. The symbol profile ("Auto" detects it) sets
//   what genuinely differs: gold CFDs and COMEX halt 17:00–18:00 New York, so on
//   timeframes up to 1H the XAUUSD profile ignores fractals whose centre bar
//   opens 16:40–18:20 New York time (BTC trades 24/7); gold prints 2 decimals,
//   BTC whole dollars.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
indicator("MTF Fractals + Stage v6", shorttitle = "MTF Fractals v6", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 50, max_labels_count = 50)

// ── Inputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
string G_PROF  = "Symbol profile"
string G_FRACT = "Fractal"
string G_STAGE = "Stage calibration"
string G_TF    = "Timeframes"
string G_DISP  = "Display"

profile = input.string("Auto", "Symbol profile", options = ["Auto", "XAUUSD", "BTCUSD", "Generic"], group = G_PROF,
     tooltip = "Auto detects XAU / GOLD / GC futures and BTC / XBT symbols. The profile only sets what differs between the markets: the gold rollover filter and the price format (gold 2 decimals, BTC whole dollars). All calibration inputs below apply to every profile.")

leftBars       = input.int(2, "Bars left",            minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_FRACT)
rightBars      = input.int(2, "Bars right (confirm)", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_FRACT)
tieLeft        = input.bool(true, "Allow equal highs / lows on the left side", group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "On: equal highs / lows are tolerated anywhere in the left window, so the newest bar of a plateau or of a tight double top / bottom tied to the tick registers as the fractal (looser than the built-in Williams Fractal, which caps the plateau at 4 bars). Off: strict on both sides, as in the v5 script, so a tied extreme never prints a fractal.")
rolloverMode   = input.string("Auto", "Ignore gold rollover-window fractals", options = ["Auto", "On", "Off"], group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "Gold CFDs and COMEX halt 17:00-18:00 New York; bars around the halt and the Sunday open print isolated extremes that are not tradable levels. On timeframes up to 1H, fractals whose centre bar opens 16:40-18:20 New York time are ignored. Auto = on for the XAUUSD profile only.")
chartCloseOnly = input.bool(true, "Chart-TF signals on bar close only", group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "On: the Chart row confirms a fractal, updates its level and stage, draws the mark and fires the 'Chart up/dn fractal' and 'Chart swing high/low broken' alerts only once the chart bar has closed (equivalent to 'Once per bar close'). Off: v5 behaviour, a fractal can be confirmed intrabar and vanish if the bar's high/low later moves. Higher-TF rows always use completed bars.")

bandMode   = input.string("ATR", "Band mode", options = ["ATR", "Percent"], group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "ATR: bands are multiples of ATR (recommended). Percent: band and buffer are a fixed % of the level on every timeframe (the v5 width); the retest and break logic is the same in both modes.")
atrLen     = input.int(14,    "ATR length",            minval = 2,    maxval = 100,              group = G_STAGE)
retestMul  = input.float(0.50, "Retest band (× ATR)",  minval = 0.05, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.05, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Multiplied by the geometric mean of the row's ATR and the chart ATR, so higher-TF bands shrink toward the chart's scale; never narrower than the row's break buffer. On the Chart row it is simply × ATR.")
breakMul   = input.float(0.15, "Break buffer (× ATR)", minval = 0.0,  maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "This TF's close must exceed the level by this much (of the row's own ATR) to count as Broken, and must close back through it by the same amount for a Failed break.")
minBufPct  = input.float(0.012, "Min break buffer (% of level, ATR mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.002, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Floor under the ATR break buffer so a close inside the spread never counts as Broken when ATR collapses in thin sessions. 0.012 % ≈ $0.50 on $4,200 gold, ≈ $9 on $77,000 BTC (negligible next to its ATR buffer).")
retestPct  = input.float(0.15,  "Retest band % (Percent mode)",  minval = 0.01, step = 0.01,  group = G_STAGE)
breakPct   = input.float(0.045, "Break buffer % (Percent mode)", minval = 0.0,  step = 0.005, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Fixed % of the level on every timeframe (3/10 of the Percent retest band, the same ratio as the ATR defaults). Set 0 for any close through the level to count (v5 had no buffer; Broken still stays until a Failed break or a new fractal).")
maxAge     = input.int(0, "Expire level N bars after confirmation (0 = never)", minval = 0, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Counted in bars of the level's own timeframe, starting at the bar that confirms the fractal; the level is removed on the Nth bar. The table tooltip shows age from the fractal's centre bar (for higher-TF rows, as of that TF's last completed bar), which is 'Bars right' larger.")

useChart = input.bool(true,  "Chart TF", group = G_TF, inline = "tf1")
use5     = input.bool(false, "5m",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf1")
use15    = input.bool(true,  "15m",      group = G_TF, inline = "tf1", tooltip = "A row is shown only when its length is above the chart length and a whole multiple of it. 5m: on 1m and seconds charts that divide 5 minutes (hidden on 2m / 3m / 4m). 15m: on 1m, 3m, 5m and such seconds charts (hidden on 2m, 4m, 10m). Hidden rows are listed in the Σ row tooltip.")
use60    = input.bool(true,  "1H",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
use240   = input.bool(true,  "4H",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
useD     = input.bool(true,  "Daily",    group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
useW     = input.bool(true,  "Weekly",   group = G_TF, inline = "tf2", tooltip = "1H: hidden on 45m charts. 4H: hidden on 45m and 3H charts. Weekly is the only higher-TF row available on a D chart and needs at least 5 weekly bars of loaded history.")

showMarks    = input.bool(true,  "Plot fractal marks",             group = G_DISP)
showStageTbl = input.bool(true,  "Stage table",                    group = G_DISP)
showLabels   = input.bool(true,  "Labels on last chart fractals",  group = G_DISP)
showLines    = input.bool(true,  "Level lines (chart TF)",         group = G_DISP)
showHtfLines = input.bool(false, "Level lines (higher TFs)",       group = G_DISP)
showBiasBg   = input.bool(false, "Background tint from MTF bias",  group = G_DISP)
tblPos       = input.string("top_right", "Table position", options = ["top_left", "top_right", "bottom_left", "bottom_right"], group = G_DISP)
bullCol      = input.color(color.new(color.teal, 0), "Bull", group = G_DISP, inline = "col")
bearCol      = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0),  "Bear", group = G_DISP, inline = "col")

// ── Profile resolution (all "simple" values: fixed for the whole run) ────────
string tick     = str.upper(syminfo.ticker)
string root     = str.upper(syminfo.root)
bool   isFut    = syminfo.type == "futures"
bool   isEq     = syminfo.type == "stock" or syminfo.type == "fund"
bool   symGold  = str.contains(tick, "XAU") or (str.contains(tick, "GOLD") and not isEq) or (isFut and (root == "GC" or root == "MGC"))
bool   symBtc   = ((str.startswith(tick, "BTC") or str.startswith(tick, "XBT")) and not isEq and not str.endswith(tick, ".D")) or (isFut and (root == "BTC" or root == "MBT"))
string resolved = profile == "Auto" ? (symGold ? "XAUUSD" : symBtc ? "BTCUSD" : "Generic") : profile
bool   rollOn   = rolloverMode == "On" or (rolloverMode == "Auto" and resolved == "XAUUSD")
string pxFmt    = resolved == "XAUUSD" ? "0.00" : resolved == "BTCUSD" ? "0" : format.mintick
bool   useAtrBand = bandMode == "ATR"
int    chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.isticks ? "1" : timeframe.period)

// ── Band helpers (price units) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
breakBuf(float lvl, float atrV) =>
    useAtrBand ? math.max(breakMul * atrV, lvl * minBufPct / 100.0) : lvl * breakPct / 100.0

retestBand(float lvl, float bandAtr) =>
    useAtrBand ? retestMul * bandAtr : lvl * retestPct / 100.0

// ── Williams fractal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
isUpFractal() =>
    bool ok = bar_index >= leftBars + rightBars
    float mid = high[rightBars]
    if ok
        for i = 0 to leftBars + rightBars
            if i < rightBars and high[i] >= mid
                ok := false
            if i > rightBars and (tieLeft ? high[i] > mid : high[i] >= mid)
                ok := false
    ok

isDnFractal() =>
    bool ok = bar_index >= leftBars + rightBars
    float mid = low[rightBars]
    if ok
        for i = 0 to leftBars + rightBars
            if i < rightBars and low[i] <= mid
                ok := false
            if i > rightBars and (tieLeft ? low[i] < mid : low[i] <= mid)
                ok := false
    ok

// ── Per-TF level engine (runs inside each request.security context) ──────────
// Returns, for the bar `off` bars ago: the last fractal level of each side, this
// TF's ATR, whether a fractal confirmed on that bar, the age of each level in
// bars of this TF (from the fractal's centre bar), the open time of each
// fractal's centre bar, the break state of each level judged on this TF's own
// close (0 intact · 1 broken · 2 failed break), and how many bars this context
// has. off = 1 together with lookahead_on is the standard non-repainting
// higher-TF pattern. tfSec is the TF length in seconds, passed in so the
// rollover filter never depends on how timeframe.in_seconds() behaves inside a
// request. gate = false postpones a confirmation (used by the Chart row to wait
// for the bar close); history is unaffected because every historical bar is
// confirmed.
tfEngine(simple int off, simple int tfSec, bool gate) =>
    float atrRma  = ta.atr(atrLen)
    float atrSeed = ta.cum(ta.tr(true)) / (bar_index + 1)   // expanding mean while the RMA warms up
    float atrV    = na(atrRma) ? atrSeed : atrRma
    int   nBars   = bar_index + 1
    int   rollT   = na
    if rollOn and tfSec <= 3600 and not timeframe.isticks
        rollT := time(timeframe.period, "1640-1820:1234567", "America/New_York")
    bool  inRoll  = not na(rollT)
    bool  upNow   = isUpFractal() and not inRoll[rightBars] and gate
    bool  dnNow   = isDnFractal() and not inRoll[rightBars] and gate
    var float lastUp = na
    var float lastDn = na
    var int   upAge  = 0
    var int   dnAge  = 0
    var int   upT    = na
    var int   dnT    = na
    var int   upB    = 0
    var int   dnB    = 0
    if upNow
        lastUp := high[rightBars]
        upAge  := rightBars
        upT    := time[rightBars]
        upB    := 0
    else
        upAge += 1
    if dnNow
        lastDn := low[rightBars]
        dnAge  := rightBars
        dnT    := time[rightBars]
        dnB    := 0
    else
        dnAge += 1
    if maxAge > 0
        if upAge - rightBars >= maxAge
            lastUp := na
            upT    := na
            upB    := 0
        if dnAge - rightBars >= maxAge
            lastDn := na
            dnT    := na
            dnB    := 0
    if not upNow and not na(lastUp)
        float bufUp = breakBuf(lastUp, atrV)
        if close > lastUp + bufUp
            upB := 1
        else if upB == 1 and close < lastUp - bufUp
            upB := 2
    if not dnNow and not na(lastDn)
        float bufDn = breakBuf(lastDn, atrV)
        if close < lastDn - bufDn
            dnB := 1
        else if dnB == 1 and close > lastDn + bufDn
            dnB := 2
    [lastUp[off], lastDn[off], atrV[off], upNow[off], dnNow[off], upAge[off], dnAge[off], upT[off], dnT[off], upB[off], dnB[off], nBars[off]]

// ── Stage machine (chart side, one independent instance per call site) ───────
//   st     : 0 none · 1 Confirmed · 2 Retest · 3 Broken · 4 Holding · 5 Flip retest · 6 Failed break
//   bstate : break state from the engine (this TF's close vs level ± buffer)
//   armed  : after a break, a chart bar has been entirely outside the retest band at least once
//   away   : since the level printed, a chart bar has been entirely outside the band at least once (a break also counts)
//   t      : open time of the fractal's centre bar; a change means a new level
sideStage(float lvl, float atrV, float chartAtr, bool hit, int t, int bstate) =>
    var bool armed = false
    var bool away  = false
    bool fresh = not na(t) and (na(t[1]) or t != t[1])
    if fresh or na(lvl)
        armed := false
        away  := false
    int st = 0
    if not na(lvl)
        float buf  = breakBuf(lvl, atrV)
        float band = math.max(retestBand(lvl, math.sqrt(atrV * chartAtr)), buf)   // the near zone always covers the buffer zone
        bool near  = high >= lvl - band and low <= lvl + band                     // chart bar range reaches into the band
        bool newBreak = bstate == 1 and bstate[1] != 1
        if newBreak
            armed := false
        if bstate == 1 and not near
            armed := true
        if not near or bstate != 0
            away := true
        if bstate == 1
            st := armed and near ? 5 : 3
        else if bstate == 2
            st := near ? 2 : 6
        else if hit and not (near and away)
            st := 1
        else if near and away
            st := 2
        else
            st := 4
    st

stageName(int s) =>
    switch s
        1 => "Confirmed"
        2 => "Retest"
        3 => "Broken"
        4 => "Holding"
        5 => "Flip retest"
        6 => "Failed break"
        => "—"

stageColor(int s) =>
    switch s
        1 => color.yellow
        2 => color.orange
        3 => color.red
        4 => color.lime
        5 => color.fuchsia
        6 => color.gray
        => color.gray

// Rows lower than the chart TF would only see the last intrabar of each chart
// bar; a row equal to the chart TF would be the Chart row one bar late (the
// engine runs on completed bars); a row that is not a whole multiple of the
// chart TF can differ between history and real time on the chart bar that
// straddles its close; tick charts have no time length to compare.
tfNote(simple string tf) =>
    int s = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    timeframe.isticks ? "tick chart" : s < chartSec ? "< chart" : s == chartSec ? "= chart" : s % chartSec != 0 ? "not a multiple" : ""

string n5   = tfNote("5")
string n15  = tfNote("15")
string n60  = tfNote("60")
string n240 = tfNote("240")
string nD   = tfNote("D")
string nW   = tfNote("W")
bool   v5   = n5 == ""
bool   v15  = n15 == ""
bool   v60  = n60 == ""
bool   v240 = n240 == ""
bool   vD   = nD == ""
bool   vW   = nW == ""

// A row that is off or hidden is never read, so its request is pointed at the
// weekly series (a few hundred bars on any symbol) instead of loading and
// processing the full intraday history for nothing. All gates are simple, so
// each request runs on every bar or never, and the engine state stays consistent.
string tf5   = use5   and v5   ? "5"   : "W"
string tf15  = use15  and v15  ? "15"  : "W"
string tf60  = use60  and v60  ? "60"  : "W"
string tf240 = use240 and v240 ? "240" : "W"
string tfD   = useD   and vD   ? "D"   : "W"

// ── Chart TF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool chartGate = not chartCloseOnly or barstate.isconfirmed
[cUpL, cDnL, cAtr, cUpHit, cDnHit, cUpAge, cDnAge, cUpT, cDnT, cUpB, cDnB, cN] = tfEngine(0, chartSec, chartGate)
int cUpSt = sideStage(cUpL, cAtr, cAtr, cUpHit, cUpT, cUpB)
int cDnSt = sideStage(cDnL, cAtr, cAtr, cDnHit, cDnT, cDnB)

plotshape(showMarks and cUpHit, title = "Up fractal", style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.abovebar, color = bullCol, size = size.tiny, offset = -rightBars)
plotshape(showMarks and cDnHit, title = "Dn fractal", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.belowbar, color = bearCol, size = size.tiny, offset = -rightBars)

// ── Higher TFs (completed bars only) ─────────────────────────────────────────
[u5,   d5,   a5,   uh5,   dh5,   ua5,   da5,   ut5,   dt5,   ub5,   db5,   n5b]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf5,   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf5),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u15,  d15,  a15,  uh15,  dh15,  ua15,  da15,  ut15,  dt15,  ub15,  db15,  n15b]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf15,  tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf15),  true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u60,  d60,  a60,  uh60,  dh60,  ua60,  da60,  ut60,  dt60,  ub60,  db60,  n60b]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf60,  tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf60),  true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u240, d240, a240, uh240, dh240, ua240, da240, ut240, dt240, ub240, db240, n240b] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf240, tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf240), true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[uD,   dD,   aD,   uhD,   dhD,   uaD,   daD,   utD,   dtD,   ubD,   dbD,   nDb]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfD,   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tfD),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[uW,   dW,   aW,   uhW,   dhW,   uaW,   daW,   utW,   dtW,   ubW,   dbW,   nWb]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W",   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds("W"),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

int us5   = sideStage(u5,   a5,   cAtr, uh5,   ut5,   ub5)
int ds5   = sideStage(d5,   a5,   cAtr, dh5,   dt5,   db5)
int us15  = sideStage(u15,  a15,  cAtr, uh15,  ut15,  ub15)
int ds15  = sideStage(d15,  a15,  cAtr, dh15,  dt15,  db15)
int us60  = sideStage(u60,  a60,  cAtr, uh60,  ut60,  ub60)
int ds60  = sideStage(d60,  a60,  cAtr, dh60,  dt60,  db60)
int us240 = sideStage(u240, a240, cAtr, uh240, ut240, ub240)
int ds240 = sideStage(d240, a240, cAtr, dh240, dt240, db240)
int usD   = sideStage(uD,   aD,   cAtr, uhD,   utD,   ubD)
int dsD   = sideStage(dD,   aD,   cAtr, dhD,   dtD,   dbD)
int usW   = sideStage(uW,   aW,   cAtr, uhW,   utW,   ubW)
int dsW   = sideStage(dW,   aW,   cAtr, dhW,   dtW,   dbW)

// ── Row model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type Row
    string name
    bool   on
    bool   valid
    string note
    float  upL
    float  dnL
    float  atr
    int    upSt
    int    dnSt
    int    upAge
    int    dnAge
    int    upT
    int    dnT
    int    nBars

rows = array.new<Row>()
array.push(rows, Row.new("Chart", useChart, true, "",   cUpL, cDnL, cAtr, cUpSt, cDnSt, cUpAge, cDnAge, cUpT, cDnT, cN))
array.push(rows, Row.new("5m",    use5,     v5,   n5,   u5,   d5,   a5,   us5,   ds5,   ua5,   da5,   ut5,   dt5,   n5b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("15m",   use15,    v15,  n15,  u15,  d15,  a15,  us15,  ds15,  ua15,  da15,  ut15,  dt15,  n15b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("1H",    use60,    v60,  n60,  u60,  d60,  a60,  us60,  ds60,  ua60,  da60,  ut60,  dt60,  n60b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("4H",    use240,   v240, n240, u240, d240, a240, us240, ds240, ua240, da240, ut240, dt240, n240b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("D",     useD,     vD,   nD,   uD,   dD,   aD,   usD,   dsD,   uaD,   daD,   utD,   dtD,   nDb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("W",     useW,     vW,   nW,   uW,   dW,   aW,   usW,   dsW,   uaW,   daW,   utW,   dtW,   nWb))

// ── MTF bias ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// +1 per TF whose last swing HIGH is broken (price above resistance),
// −1 per TF whose last swing LOW is broken (price below support).
// Intact levels, Retest and Failed break contribute 0.
biasOf(int upS, int dnS) =>
    int b = 0
    if upS == 3 or upS == 5
        b += 1
    if dnS == 3 or dnS == 5
        b -= 1
    b

int    bias      = 0
int    nScore    = 0
string hiddenTxt = ""
for r in rows
    if r.on and r.valid
        bias   += biasOf(r.upSt, r.dnSt)
        nScore += 1
    else if r.on
        hiddenTxt += (hiddenTxt == "" ? "" : ", ") + r.name + " (" + r.note + ")"

plot(bias, "MTF fractal bias", display = display.data_window)
bgcolor(showBiasBg and bias > 0 ? color.new(bullCol, 92) : showBiasBg and bias < 0 ? color.new(bearCol, 92) : na, title = "Bias tint")

// ── Stage table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pos = switch tblPos
    "top_left"     => position.top_left
    "top_right"    => position.top_right
    "bottom_left"  => position.bottom_left
    => position.bottom_right
var table t = table.new(pos, 6, 10, bgcolor = color.new(#0d1117, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))

fmtPx(float x) =>
    na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, pxFmt)

bandText(float lvl, float atrV) =>
    float buf  = breakBuf(lvl, atrV)
    float band = math.max(retestBand(lvl, math.sqrt(atrV * cAtr)), buf)
    "ATR " + fmtPx(atrV) + "  ·  retest ±" + fmtPx(band) + "  ·  break buffer " + fmtPx(buf)

paintRow(int row, Row r) =>
    int b = biasOf(r.upSt, r.dnSt)
    bool tooShort = r.nBars < leftBars + rightBars + 1
    string shortTxt = "only " + str.tostring(r.nBars) + " bars"
    string ageNote  = r.name == "Chart" ? " bars" : " bars (as of last closed " + r.name + " bar)"
    table.cell(t, 0, row, r.name, text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, row, fmtPx(r.upL), text_color = bullCol, text_size = size.small, tooltip = na(r.upL) ? "" : bandText(r.upL, r.atr) + "  ·  age " + str.tostring(r.upAge) + ageNote)
    table.cell(t, 2, row, na(r.upL) and tooShort ? shortTxt : stageName(r.upSt), text_color = stageColor(r.upSt), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 3, row, fmtPx(r.dnL), text_color = bearCol, text_size = size.small, tooltip = na(r.dnL) ? "" : bandText(r.dnL, r.atr) + "  ·  age " + str.tostring(r.dnAge) + ageNote)
    table.cell(t, 4, row, na(r.dnL) and tooShort ? shortTxt : stageName(r.dnSt), text_color = stageColor(r.dnSt), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 5, row, b > 0 ? "+1" : b < 0 ? "−1" : "0", text_color = b > 0 ? bullCol : b < 0 ? bearCol : color.gray, text_size = size.small)

if showStageTbl and barstate.islast
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "TF",       text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, "Swing hi", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 2, 0, "Stage",    text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 3, 0, "Swing lo", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 4, 0, "Stage",    text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 5, 0, "Bias",     text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    int rowIdx = 1
    for r in rows
        if r.on and r.valid
            paintRow(rowIdx, r)
            rowIdx += 1
    string profTxt = resolved + (rollOn ? " · rollover filter" : "") + "  L" + str.tostring(leftBars) + "/R" + str.tostring(rightBars) + (useAtrBand ? "  ATR" + str.tostring(atrLen) + " ×" + str.tostring(retestMul) + "/" + str.tostring(breakMul) : "  " + str.tostring(retestPct) + "%/" + str.tostring(breakPct) + "%")
    string sumTip  = "Sum of the per-TF bias over the enabled, usable timeframes." + (hiddenTxt == "" ? "" : "  Hidden: " + hiddenTxt + ". A row must be higher than the chart timeframe and a whole multiple of it; the Chart row covers the chart timeframe.")
    table.cell(t, 0, rowIdx, "Σ", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, rowIdx, profTxt, text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, tooltip = "Symbol profile · fractal left/right · ATR length × retest multiplier / break multiplier")
    table.cell(t, 2, rowIdx, "", text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 3, rowIdx, "", text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 4, rowIdx, "", text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 5, rowIdx, (bias > 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(bias) + " / " + str.tostring(nScore), text_color = bias > 0 ? bullCol : bias < 0 ? bearCol : color.gray, text_size = size.small, tooltip = sumTip)

// ── Labels on last chart fractals ────────────────────────────────────────────
var label upLab = na
var label dnLab = na
if showLabels and barstate.islast
    label.delete(upLab)
    label.delete(dnLab)
    if not na(cUpL)
        upLab := label.new(bar_index + 1, cUpL, "▲ " + stageName(cUpSt) + "  " + fmtPx(cUpL), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(bullCol, 75), textcolor = bullCol, size = size.small)
    if not na(cDnL)
        dnLab := label.new(bar_index + 1, cDnL, "▼ " + stageName(cDnSt) + "  " + fmtPx(cDnL), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(bearCol, 75), textcolor = bearCol, size = size.small)

// ── Level lines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var line cUpLine = na
var line cDnLine = na
if showLines and barstate.islast
    line.delete(cUpLine)
    line.delete(cDnLine)
    if not na(cUpL)
        cUpLine := line.new(math.max(bar_index - cUpAge, bar_index - 4000), cUpL, bar_index + 1, cUpL, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(bullCol, 30), style = line.style_solid, width = 1)
    if not na(cDnL)
        cDnLine := line.new(math.max(bar_index - cDnAge, bar_index - 4000), cDnL, bar_index + 1, cDnL, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(bearCol, 30), style = line.style_solid, width = 1)

// Higher-TF lines start at the open time of the fractal's centre bar.
var array<line> htfLines = array.new<line>()
if showHtfLines and barstate.islast
    for l in htfLines
        line.delete(l)
    array.clear(htfLines)
    int tEnd = time + chartSec * 1000 * 2
    for r in rows
        if r.on and r.valid and r.name != "Chart"
            if not na(r.upL) and not na(r.upT)
                array.push(htfLines, line.new(r.upT, r.upL, tEnd, r.upL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bullCol, 55), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1))
            if not na(r.dnL) and not na(r.dnT)
                array.push(htfLines, line.new(r.dnT, r.dnL, tEnd, r.dnL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bearCol, 55), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1))

// ── Alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every helper is evaluated unconditionally at global scope so its [1] history
// is complete (v6 and/or short-circuit would otherwise skip calls).
enteredBroken(int st) =>
    (st == 3 or st == 5) and not (st[1] == 3 or st[1] == 5)
enteredRetest(int st) =>
    (st == 2 or st == 5) and not (st[1] == 2 or st[1] == 5)

bool cUpBrk = enteredBroken(cUpSt) and chartGate
bool cDnBrk = enteredBroken(cDnSt) and chartGate
bool cUpRt  = enteredRetest(cUpSt)
bool cDnRt  = enteredRetest(cDnSt)
bool b5u    = enteredBroken(us5)
bool b5d    = enteredBroken(ds5)
bool b15u   = enteredBroken(us15)
bool b15d   = enteredBroken(ds15)
bool b60u   = enteredBroken(us60)
bool b60d   = enteredBroken(ds60)
bool b240u  = enteredBroken(us240)
bool b240d  = enteredBroken(ds240)
bool bDu    = enteredBroken(usD)
bool bDd    = enteredBroken(dsD)
bool bWu    = enteredBroken(usW)
bool bWd    = enteredBroken(dsW)

bool htfUpBreak = (use5 and v5 and b5u) or (use15 and v15 and b15u) or (use60 and v60 and b60u) or (use240 and v240 and b240u) or (useD and vD and bDu) or (useW and vW and bWu)
bool htfDnBreak = (use5 and v5 and b5d) or (use15 and v15 and b15d) or (use60 and v60 and b60d) or (use240 and v240 and b240d) or (useD and vD and bDd) or (useW and vW and bWd)

alertcondition(cUpHit,     "Chart up fractal",        "Up fractal confirmed (chart TF) on {{ticker}}")
alertcondition(cDnHit,     "Chart dn fractal",        "Down fractal confirmed (chart TF) on {{ticker}}")
alertcondition(cUpBrk,     "Chart swing high broken", "Close above last chart swing high on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
alertcondition(cDnBrk,     "Chart swing low broken",  "Close below last chart swing low on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
alertcondition(cUpRt,      "Chart swing high retest", "Price retesting last chart swing high on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
alertcondition(cDnRt,      "Chart swing low retest",  "Price retesting last chart swing low on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
alertcondition(htfUpBreak, "HTF swing high broken",   "A higher timeframe closed above its last swing high on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
alertcondition(htfDnBreak, "HTF swing low broken",    "A higher timeframe closed below its last swing low on {{ticker}} ({{close}})")
